{"t":1370815.4596657,"req":"h07","event":"done","status":"answered","level":0,"steps":["classify","retrieve","draft"],"answer":"Moshi\u2019s Inner Monologue method generates text tokens as a prefix before producing audio tokens.  It extends hierarchical semantic\u2011to\u2011acoustic token generation by first predicting time\u2011aligned text tokens, which are then used to guide the subsequent generation of speech tokens from a neural audio codec.  This prefix\u2011text step improves linguistic quality and enables streaming speech\u2011recognition and text\u2011to\u2011speech while keeping inference latency low[C:moshi:1]."}
